From 771c40fb12d1046c47d6a94b54168ac8595178e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: handylinux <8155246+handylinux@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 07:13:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] patch 146: alert catalog and a single dialog host
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds components/alerts/: a catalog of the app's dialogs, a promise-based
service, and one AlertHost mounted in App.js.

Why: five near-identical showAlert wrappers existed (CharacterContext,
HomeScreen, InventoryScreen, CharacterScreen, PerksAndTraitsScreen) and
the Platform.OS === 'web' branch was spread over ~50 call sites. On web
those branches fell back to window.confirm/prompt, which cannot show
more than two buttons — so three-option dialogs lost an option.

The host renders a normal React modal, identical on web and native, with
any number of buttons. Domain code must not call it: pure logic returns
an event and the screen maps it to a catalog entry.

First call site converted: applying a consumable. On web its three
options used to collapse into window.confirm where 'Cancel' actually
meant 'apply to another character' — cancelling was impossible.

Catalog holds i18n keys, not strings; all keys verified present in ru-RU
and en-EN. Remaining call sites keep working unchanged and can be moved
over one screen at a time.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
